{
  "about": "Queries for the correctness benchmark. Categories are refined when the answer key is built (ccTLDs are split by whether the registry has RDAP; IPs get their RIR). 'registrable' is the domain whose registration a subdomain query should report. 'holdout' domains were added after whoq's port-43 parser was fixed against the other ccTLDs; they test whether those fixes generalize, and were hand-checked before whoq was run on them. 'fresh' domains were added after availability detection was changed in response to the holdout set, on registries used nowhere else, and were hand-checked before whoq was run on them. 'fresh2' domains were added after the port-43 parser switched from exact key spellings to classifying keys by their words; again on registries used nowhere else, hand-checked before whoq was run on them.",
